    "body": "## Completed bounded milestone\n\nReferences #973 and #820. This PR delivers the calibrated-shadow adapter and the complete, preserved result of the already authorized full-context language continuation. **The language target failed; neither new candidate is promoted.**\n\n### Actual outcome\n\n- Both continuous arms reached the sole final step **15,672**, retaining exactly **7,324 added updates / 29,999,104 target visits per arm** from step8,348. B16, training/evaluation/session256, full causal access, state256/read64, model/Adam/sampler continuity and ordinary control are preserved.\n- Continuous comparison NLL improves to **1.996490 quaternion / 1.974724 ordinary**, but actual prose remains **0/5 in each arm**. Integer prose is **0/5 quaternion / 1/5 ordinary**; all four groups miss the frozen3/5 and two-story improvement requirements. All texts, quotes, positive dimensions and reviewer disagreements are retained.\n- Ordinary fails hard-minus-continuous **0.072164 > 0.05**, original-rung1 first-noun losses **3 > 2**, and integer Read state drift **0.012695 > 0.01**. Quaternion passes the scoped F32 and integer drift/source controls, but its standalone goose story short-cycles. Against accepted integer parents, complete source answers regress **28→25 / 24→21**, with every lost/gained row preserved.\n- Fresh calibration, fixed alpha512, full F32 Read/NoRead, four-window integer comparison, bound bundles, source panels and five-story outputs all completed. Current accepted September25 artifacts remain retained; no extra exposure or promotion follows.\n\n### Decision\n\nPark exposure-only fitting. Existing traces justify prioritizing one later **same-checkpoint emission/selection causal diagnostic**. A recorded low-model-mass sampled token differs from the same-prefix greedy choice, but no alternate rollout or single cause has been established. Greedy source regressions and separate numerical failures prevent a sampling-only explanation. Full256 access and the project’s geometric goal remain unchanged; no new training, scale/admission search or decoding-policy change was executed in closeout.\n\n### Verification and preservation\n\n- Adapter: **2 focused release checks passed**, then both actual retained parents completed zero-update calibration, hard export, bound integer loading and eight-token interface exercises. Build/source/executable identities are recorded.\n- Frozen continuous and downstream reports were Rust seal-verified. Independent review parsed all eight existing F32 target streams and reconciled actual source rows. Principal and independent prose reviews used the unchanged rubric.\n- Closeout documentation: changed JSON parsing, local link targets, `git diff --check` and claim-wording check passed. No blanket test suite or repeated model run.\n- SSD snapshot: 1,082,432,690 bytes; all67 copied Rust manifest roots pass; both immutable snapshots total1,967,707,358 bytes within the original4GiB allowance. Internal free space at verification is51,746,230,272 bytes. See [closeout evidence](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/codex/language-continuation-20260925/docs/evidence/language-continuation-closeout-2026-09-26.json). This preserves the completed packet and exact source alongside the original immutable dependency snapshot; model paths and originals remain internal.\n- GitHub’s historical five check names are queue compatibility acknowledgments, **not executed tests**. Local receipts carry validation. No protection bypass.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- [Integrated result](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/codex/language-continuation-20260925/docs/integration/language-continuation-result-2026-09-26.md)\n- [Principal result](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/codex/language-continuation-20260925/docs/evidence/language-continuation-result-2026-09-26.json)\n- [All integer prose and both reviews](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/codex/language-continuation-20260925/docs/evidence/language-continuation-integer-quality-2026-09-26.json)\n- [Numerical/source adjudication](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/codex/language-continuation-20260925/docs/evidence/language-continuation-numerical-source-2026-09-26.json)\n- [Every historical source-row comparison](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/codex/language-continuation-20260925/docs/evidence/language-continuation-source-comparisons-2026-09-26.json)\n- [Trace evidence and inference limits](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/codex/language-continuation-20260925/docs/evidence/language-continuation-trace-coverage-2026-09-26.json)\n\nThe first pipe-failed fit lost its uncheckpointed updates; that loss remains explicit and charged. Later saved learning, failed candidates and owner material are preserved. Broader #973/#820 acceptance remains open.\n",
